WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.846
Sovereign AI means deliberate control over data, models, infrastructure, access, policy,

00:00:04.846 --> 00:00:05.709
and operations.

00:00:05.709 --> 00:00:10.886
It begins with data classification: know what prompts, documents, embeddings, outputs, logs,

00:00:10.886 --> 00:00:16.063
and evaluation records may contain before routing them into an AI workflow.

00:00:16.063 --> 00:00:20.378
Data sensitivity should guide deployment, retention, access, and monitoring decisions.

00:00:20.378 --> 00:00:26.418
Choose local, private, cloud, or hybrid deployment based on the work, not on slogans.

00:00:26.418 --> 00:00:29.438
Consider sensitivity, performance, cost, usability, operational capacity,

00:00:29.438 --> 00:00:30.732
and vendor commitments.

00:00:30.732 --> 00:00:36.341
Treat private RAG as a permissioned knowledge system, not just a vector database.

00:00:36.341 --> 00:00:40.655
Preserve source provenance, permissions, freshness, tenant boundaries, and lifecycle status.

00:00:40.655 --> 00:00:43.244
Scope model and tool access carefully.

00:00:43.244 --> 00:00:46.696
A model endpoint, retrieval collection, tool, agent workflow,

00:00:46.696 --> 00:00:51.441
or administrative function should have clear permissions and audit-ready policy decisions.

00:00:51.441 --> 00:00:54.893
Monitor quality and usage without over-collecting sensitive logs.

00:00:54.893 --> 00:00:58.776
Evaluation, observability, and privacy controls should reinforce each other.

00:00:58.776 --> 00:01:03.090
Finally, plan for infrastructure cost, reliability, backup, recovery, and governance.

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:06.973
Define owners for models, vendors, retrieval collections, policy, incidents,

00:01:06.973 --> 00:01:08.268
and change control.

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:12.582
A sovereign AI program succeeds when control is practical, visible,

00:01:12.582 --> 00:01:15.171
and maintainable across everyday engineering work.

00:01:15.171 --> 00:01:18.622
The durable habit is to make control visible.

00:01:18.622 --> 00:01:24.231
Teams should be able to point to the data rule, the deployment choice,

00:01:24.231 --> 00:01:29.408
the approved model, the retrieval boundary, the tool permission, the monitoring decision,

00:01:29.408 --> 00:01:30.703
and the owner.

00:01:30.703 --> 00:01:33.723
When those decisions are documented and reviewable,

00:01:33.723 --> 00:01:38.900
sovereign AI becomes a repeatable operating model instead of a one-off experiment.
